 outcome in patients with acute renal failure</article-title><source>Crit Care</source><year>2008</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>R74</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18533029</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B5"><label>5</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bouchard</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Mehta</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fluid balance issues in the critically ill patient</article-title><source>Contrib Nephrol</source><year>2010</year><volume>164</volume><fpage>69</fpage><lpage>78</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">20427995</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B6"><label>6</label><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schetz</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Assessment of volume status</article-title><source>Critical Care Nephrology</source><year>2009</year><edition>2nd ed</edition><publisher-loc>Philadelphia</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Saunders</publisher-name><fpage>499</fpage><lpage>504</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="B7"><label>7</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Funk</surname><given-names>GC</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindner</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Druml</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Incidence and prognosis of dysnatremias present on ICU admission</article-title><source>Intensive Care Med</source><year>2010</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>304</fpage><lpage>311</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">19847398</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stelfox</surname><given-names>HT</given-names></name><name>